        "textAlign": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "10. Conclusion",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "QSAR remains one of the most influential computational methodologies in chemical and biological sciences.When implementing QSAR with meticulous validation, careful descriptor selection, and a keen understanding of its constraints, it offers invaluable predictive capabilities that expedite the processes of drug discovery and chemical risk evaluation.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "With thorough validation, precise descriptor selection, and a clear grasp of its constraints, QSAR offers indispensable predictive capabilities that expedite drug discovery and enhance chemical risk assessment. ",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
        "textAlign": null
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "However, QSAR should be viewed as a ",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "decision-support tool",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ", not a replacement for experimental validation. Future advancements in machine learning and explainable AI are expected to further enhance the reliability and acceptance of QSAR models.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
